      "text": [
        " : سَأَلْتُهُ عَنِ اَلْمَرْأَةِ اَلْمُوسِرَةِ قَدْ حَجَّتْ حَجَّةَ اَلْإِسْلاَمِ فَتَقُولُ لِزَوْجِهَا أَ حِجَّنِي مَرَّةً أُخْرَى أَ لَهُ أَنْ يَمْنَعَهَا قَالَ «نَعَمْ يَقُولُ لَهَا حَقِّي عَلَيْكِ أَعْظَمُ مِنْ حَقِّكِ عَلَيَّ فِي ذَا »."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2909 - Ishaq ibn Ammar narrated from Abu Ibrahim (as), who said:\nI asked him about a wealthy woman who had already performed the Hajj of Islam but said to her husband, \"Take me for Hajj again.\" Can he prevent her from going?\nImam (as) said: \"Yes, he can say to her, 'My right over you is greater than your right over me in this matter.'\""
        ]
      }
